  Confirm the fix                                                               
  ~/.ssh has mode 0755 offers one deterministic change, and this is exactly     
  it. Nothing else on the machine is touched.                                   
  before: /home/testuser/.ssh has mode 0755                                     
  after:  /home/testuser/.ssh has mode 0700                                     
  Risk: A mode that is too open is a way into every tool that reads this path,  
  and OpenSSH refuses to use a key inside a directory others can read.          
  Permission needed: Ownership of /home/testuser/.ssh; no administrator rights  
  are needed when this user owns it.                                            
  Backup: The mode it has now (0755) is written into the fix record with the    
  command that puts it back: `chmod 0755 /home/testuser/.ssh`.                  
  Press a to apply it, or Escape to leave without changing anything.            
                                                                                
  ▸ [a] Set the mode to 0700                                                    
    ← Back                                                                      
                                                                                
                                                                                
                                                                                
                                                                                
